meta {
  name: Unlink Category from Product
  type: http
  seq: 18
}

delete {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID/categories/REPLACE_WITH_CATEGORY_ID
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  `DELETE /api/v3/products/{product_id}/categories/{category_id}` — remove one
  category from a product, leaving the product and its other categories intact.
  Confirmed live 2026-10-08 against "David's Dev Account" on a disposable product
  (`WC-REV-1008-A`) that had two categories linked; since deleted.

  ## This is now a SAFE, SCOPED unlink — the hazard is fully gone
  This exact path has a long history in this collection. It was originally
  confirmed **destructive** (quirk #54, 2026-09-11: it deleted the entire
  product), then **safe but non-functional** (2026-09-23: `404 "Product has no
  field 'categories/<id>'"`). **As of 2026-10-08 it works as intended**: `204`,
  and a follow-up `GET /products/{id}` shows the product fully intact — `sku`,
  `label`, `status` and `attributes` all unchanged — with only the named category
  removed and the other one still attached. Verified in the same run.

  This is the second confirmed safe scoped unlink in v3, after
  `DELETE /products/{id}/relationships/{relationship_id}` (quirk #62). It
  implements the "1:M unlink an entity instance" row that
  `materials/api-references/API V3 - status map (08_10_2026).md` marks **Direct**
  (pp. 11-13).

  ## Why you need this: `category_ids` no longer works
  The previously-documented removal method — `PATCH /products/{id}` with a
  reduced `category_ids` array — is **rejected** as of 2026-10-08 with
  `422 "category_ids: Extra inputs are not permitted"` (quirk #93). This endpoint
  is now the only way to remove a category from a product via the API.

  ## Sibling paths and their errors (all confirmed non-destructive)
  - `DELETE /products/{id}/categories` (bare collection) → `405`
    `{"name":"MethodNotAllowed","description":"DELETE on 'categories' requires
    exactly one linked id: DELETE /products/{id}/categories/{linked_id}"}`
  - `DELETE /products/{id}/<unrecognized>` → `404`
    `{"name":"NotFoundError","description":"Product has no field '<unrecognized>'"}`
  - `PATCH /products/{id}/categories` → `405`
    `{"name":"MethodNotAllowed","description":"PATCH is not allowed on
    'categories': link or unlink here, and update a linked entity at its own
    path."}`

  The product survived all three, confirmed by follow-up `GET`.

  ## Not available for assets
  `DELETE /products/{id}/assets/{asset_id}` returns `404 "Product has no field
  'assets/<id>'"` — assets do not support this pattern (quirk #96). With
  `category_ids`-style arrays gone, there is currently **no** way to detach a
  non-thumbnail asset from a product.
}

example {
  name: Unlink Category - 204 No Content
  description: Real response captured 2026-10-08 against "David's Dev Account". Product WC-REV-1008-A had two categories; this removed only "WC Test Category" and left "WC Test Child Category" attached.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa/categories/6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc
    method: delete
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 204
      text: No Content
    }
    headers: {}
    body: {
      type: text
      content: ''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Verify After Unlink - Product Intact, One Category Left
  description: Follow-up GET captured 2026-10-08 immediately after the 204 above, proving the unlink is scoped and the product survived.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa/categories
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {"data": [{"id": "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd", "name": "WC Test Child Category", "parent_id": "6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "path": ["WC Test Category", "WC Test Child Category"], "slug": "wc-test-child-category", "order": 1, "n_children": 0}], "errors": [], "pagination": {}}
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Unlink Category - 405 Bare Collection
  description: Real response captured 2026-10-08, omitting the category id. Non-destructive; the product was confirmed intact afterwards.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6ac7ef509c6194f8c08e24aa/categories
    method: delete
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 405
      text: Method Not Allowed
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {"data": [], "errors": [{"name": "MethodNotAllowed", "description": "DELETE on 'categories' requires exactly one linked id: DELETE /products/{id}/categories/{linked_id}"}]}
      '''
    }
  }
}
